# Era 5 — Projects & Configuration (V14–V17)

_Phase 2 · Concept Layer V1_

**Status: ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17**

**Implementation note:** `concepts/projects.mdx` (V14), `concepts/configuration.mdx` (V15,
two-pass disclosure applied), and `concepts/building-applications.mdx` (V17) written new. V16
(Environments and variables) resolved per Era 1's classification: `deploying/environment-variables.mdx`
already covers this topic adequately (redeploy triggers, secrets handling) — no content
change needed at Phase 2 altitude; promoting it into the Concepts nav group is Era 12's job,
not this era's. Every page's "Projects"/"Configuration" cross-link verified to resolve.

Covers T9–T12: Projects, Configuration, Environments and variables, Building applications.

---

## V14 — Projects (T9)

### Goal
New concept page: creating/selecting projects, linking a local repository, accepted names
and IDs, multiple applications in one project, deletion consequences.

### Reuses
`cli/project.mdx` as reference target; links back to `how-beaver-fits-together.mdx` (V6)
and forward to Integrations (V10) for the repo-linking sub-topic rather than re-explaining it.

### Implement
`concepts/projects.mdx` per template. Deletion consequences stated plainly (what's
irreversible) — this page is a natural candidate for a `<Warning>` component per
`components.txt`.

### Validate
No duplication with V10's repo-linking content — one explanation, cross-linked.

### Done when
Page exists.

---

## V15 — Configuration (T10)

### Goal
New concept page: what belongs in `.beaver/`, the supported YAML fields at a conceptual
level, local vs. stored configuration, push/pull/status, revisions, conflicts, backups, and
how operational commands (deploy, scale, etc.) affect configuration.

### Reuses
`cli/config.mdx` as reference target. This is flagged in the sibling roadmap's own inventory
as the **highest flag-density family** (55 flag sites) — this concept page must stay at
"what a config revision is and why you'd care," never drift into field-by-field syntax,
which is exactly what `cli/config.mdx` (or its Era 9 split pages) already owns.

### Implement
`concepts/configuration.mdx`: local-vs-stored as the core mental model, what a "conflict"
means to a user (two sides differ; here's how you see that) without describing the
diff/reconcile mechanism (checkpoint terms: `reconcile`, `drift`, `desired state` — same
list as the sibling roadmap's `DISCLOSURE.md`, directly relevant here since `config` and
`statecmd`/`projectcontract` share this vocabulary).

### Validate
Two-read disclosure pass — this page sits directly adjacent to the sibling roadmap's
highest-disclosure-risk families (`statecmd`, `projectcontract`, Era 9 there).

### Done when
Page exists, stays at concept altitude (Invariant 1), passes two-read disclosure.

