## V16 — Environments and variables (T11)

### Goal
New concept page: separating dev/staging/production, override precedence, `.env` files,
remote variables, handling secrets, when changes require a redeploy.

### Reuses
`deploying/environment-variables.mdx` (already exists under "Deploying with Docker") as the
closest existing content — check whether it's task-guide-shaped or already concept-shaped;
if the latter, this may be a **merge target promoted into the new Concepts group** rather
than a net-new page (a live classification refinement to confirm at write time, logged here
either way).

### Implement
Either extend `deploying/environment-variables.mdx` in place and link it from the new
Concepts group's index, or write `concepts/environments-and-variables.mdx` and have
`deploying/environment-variables.mdx` link up to it for the conceptual framing while keeping
its own Docker-build-specific detail. Decide based on the actual gap found, not guessed here.

### Validate
No duplicate "what is an environment variable override" explanation across two pages.

### Done when
The precedence rules and redeploy-trigger conditions are explained once, at concept level,
and linked from wherever a user would land looking for either page.

