## V17 — Building applications (T12)

### Goal
New concept page: supported runtimes/frameworks (Docker-required, bring-your-own-Dockerfile
model per `CLAUDE.md`'s current positioning), build context and paths, image naming,
private images, builder selection, diagnosing build failures — at concept level.

### Reuses
`deploying/dockerfile-requirements.mdx`, `languages/*.mdx`, `runtimes/*.mdx`,
`frameworks/*.mdx` — all already reflect the current "Dockerfile required" model per
`CLAUDE.md`. This page is the connective "why Dockerfile-first, what that means for you"
explanation those pages individually assume the reader already has.

### Implement
`concepts/building-applications.mdx`: states the bring-your-own-Dockerfile model plainly
(this is product positioning, already public, not a disclosure risk), links to
`deploying/dockerfile-requirements.mdx` for the exact requirements and to the relevant
`languages/*.mdx` page per stack. Diagnosing build failures section stays at the observable
level (what error classes look like to a user) and links to Troubleshooting (T33, Era 11)
rather than duplicating recovery steps.

### Validate
Confirms no auto-detection/auto-dockerization language leaks in (the CLAUDE.md-flagged
previous-model language) — a straightforward correctness check, not a disclosure check.

### Done when
Page exists and correctly reflects current (not historical) product positioning.
